{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110753","id":2847268914,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6pteAy","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110753","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110753.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110753.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110753","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110753/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110753/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110753/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a300e3516aba7b47b4341be530728656aab43495","number":110753,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Add support for @abstract annotation with vars","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"* requires/includes #93787 \r\n* closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13218\r\n\r\nDraft for now as dicussion is still underway on the proposal, but should be ready for merge if/when approved.\r\n\r\nAdds support for using the `@abstract` annotation with variables within `@abstract` classes. \r\nThis annotation requires that the variable it is attached to gets given an initial value by child classes using `@override`. \r\nFor more details on `@override`, please check #93787. tldr: `@override` enables the user to specialize an initial value for a variable which is not impacted by the setter. \r\n\r\nThis does not automatically make the setter and getter abstract. \r\n\r\nBasic usage example:\r\n```GDScript\r\n@abstract class Animal:\r\n  @abstract var legs: int # Every class that extends animal must give this an initial value\r\n\r\nclass Cat extends Animal:\r\n  @override var legs: int = 4 # Sets the initial value for Animal.legs to 4\r\n\r\n# Stork will be considered incomplete since it doesn't give a value for legs, \r\n# and will throw an analyzer error (won't let you compile/run). \r\nclass Stork extends Animal:\r\n  var feathers: int = 10000\r\n```\r\n\r\nTechnically speaking, this requires that the child class defines the initializer for the field, as opposed to the current behavior where the base class is responsible for defining this initializer (which is also optional in GDScript).\r\nThis has two benefits:\r\n* The initializer does not go through the setter, meaning its value stored as-is without any chance of being modified\r\n* Makes giving an initial value to the variable a requirement for child class completeness, which is a development safety feature to ensure all child classes define an initial value that is appropriate for their use","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archiv